# Licence

This repository is licensed in two parts, because it holds two different
kinds of work.

## The source code — MIT

Everything except `content/` and `public/audio/` is under the MIT licence
below: `src/`, `scripts/`, the workflows, the configuration and the
documentation. Take it, learn from it, build on it.

## The language content — not MIT

`content/` and `public/audio/` are **not** covered by the MIT licence. They
are the phrases, translations, scenarios and recordings that make up the
product, and they are all rights reserved. See
[LICENSE-CONTENT](LICENSE-CONTENT).

